00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:07.110 align:start position:0%
there is a weighty agenda for eu leaders  when they gather for the spring summit  in brussels on the 19th and 20th of  march  the first topic will be the energy union  europe needs to secure its energy  supplies and requires affordable energy  as well as climate friendly energy  all of which are equally important  at this summit the president of the  european council donald tusk wants  leaders to focus on energy security and  the internal energy market  one element of the discussion for  example will be transparency in the gas  market  as witnessed in the last few years  overdependence on one gas supplier  weakens the eu and its member states  geopolitically but also economically  eu leaders will also prepare for the  upcoming eastern partnership summit in  riga in may  the eu wants to underline its commitment  to and reinforce its relations with the  six eastern partners ukraine belarus the  republic of moldova armenia azerbaijan  and georgia  on russia and ukraine leaders will  discuss the link between the existing  sanctions and the full implementations  of all the points in the minsk  agreements brokered by president  hollande and chancellor merkel  on the second day of the summit the  situation in libya will be addressed  the critical situation is already a  tragedy for the libyan population and  poses serious challenges in terms of  migration and terrorism for europe  as regards the transatlantic trade and  investment partnership the eu-us trade  talks eu leaders will take stock of the  progress so far  they will reiterate their december 2014  summit pledge to see the deal concluded  by the end of 2015.  the european council will then discuss  the european economy and reconfirm the  three main pillars of its strategy  investments reforms and sound public  finances
 

